                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the brand & define the position`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Cordillera Verde sources <strong>100% of its green coffee from certified Tarrazú cooperatives</strong> and pays a verified farmer premium — yet aided awareness is just <strong>31%</strong> against the rival's 58%, equity sits at 42/100, and the price premium has compressed from 35% to 22%. You own the category's best sustainability story and have wasted it. Diagnose where you are losing and craft a position: pick the target segment and a point of difference. <em>If you removed the sustainability line and your positioning didn't change, you don't have one.</em> Anchor it on proof points that are real and defensible.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Choose the sustainable-marketing campaign`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Design the campaign that carries the position. The tension is real: <strong>bold, broad "eco" claims</strong> move perception fast but invite a greenwashing complaint and a credibility collapse; <strong>specific, verified claims</strong> ("100% certified sourcing, farmer premium paid") build durable trust more slowly. Choose the claim architecture, the proof mechanism that substantiates it, and how far past your evidence you are willing to push. <em>You have a true story — overclaim past it and you greenwash; whisper it and you waste it.</em>`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Allocate the ₡480M media budget`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `The decisive round. Split <strong>CRC 480M</strong> across TV/streaming (reach), digital/social (targeting + storytelling), retail/trade (conversion, but it eats margin), influencer/PR (credibility) and D2C (high conversion, scales slowly). The <strong>18% contribution-margin floor binds</strong>: trade spend lifts sell-through but compresses margin, and pouring everything into mass-reach TV builds famous-but-unprofitable vanity reach. There is an optional <strong>AI-personalization layer</strong> — a co-pilot to sharpen segments and the mix, not the captain. <em>Reach without conversion is vanity; where does the equity actually convert to sales?</em>`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — The board review & equity trajectory`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Present the integrated plan to the board. Show the four-quarter trajectory for <strong>awareness, brand equity, campaign ROI and sustainability perception</strong> — and prove margin stayed above 18%. Report honestly: you cannot credibly claim awareness up 20, equity up 18, top sustainability perception AND positive ROI on CRC 480M — <em>the reach math won't support all four</em>. Defend the price premium on equity, not discount, and prove the positioning-campaign-media logic is one coherent system. If equity and perception haven't moved and margin slipped, the brand is repositioned downmarket — permanently.`,

                    r1_segment_label:       `Choose the target segment to anchor the positioning.`,
                    r1_position_label:      `What is Cordillera Verde's point of difference?`,
                    r1_proof_label:         `How real and specific are the sustainability proof points you build the position on? (0–100)`,
                    r1_proof_readout:       `Verifiable proof anchored in the position:`,
                    seg_conscious:          `Conscious premium drinkers — shoppers who already pay for quality and will pay more for a credible sustainability story`,
                    seg_mass:               `Everyone who buys coffee — go broad, don't narrow the brand to a niche`,
                    seg_price:              `Price-sensitive trade-down shoppers — win back the people leaving for private label on price`,
                    seg_rivalfans:          `The rival's buyers — out-spend the multinational head-on for its own audience`,
                    pos_core:               `Sustainability is the meaning — the only Costa Rican coffee sourced 100% from certified cooperatives at a verified farmer premium`,
